From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Astall <aa@clhoz.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host/friends: accept presence instead of failing it

UserPresence::Initialize, SetDescription and Commit now succeed and
publish nothing. They returned RES_FAIL like the calls that need the
friends service.

Twelve Minutes (Unity 2019.4 IL2CPP, SDK 12.3.7) calls Initialize once
after account::GetNickname. On a failure its start-up stops before
fs::MountSaveData, so the loading screen stays at 22% while the music
plays (seedds/nxnative#217). With presence accepted it mounts its save
and loads the next scenes within a second.

The calls that need the service (friend lists, notification queue,
online play sessions, invitations) still fail. t_friends checks both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2903
Reason: Twelve Minutes stops at 22% when the host fails friends presence; bridge until upstream merges
Issue: none (seedds/nxnative#217)

